--- body ---
## Context

Stage 4 for one-off documents, where no repeated series justifies a parser
(the nine plans and approval documents of [[1505]], most project pages and
news of [[1504]]). Phase M2.3 of [[1500]], the reading lane. The normative
text is `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 6.3 of the accepted specification v1 (tag
`jetp-spec-v1`); this ticket builds it and does not restate it. Related:
§ 5 (locators derived from the quote), § 12 (red tests and controls), § 15
(checks), `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 5 (where each reader runs, what reaches
a hosted model), `docs/jetp-requirements.md` Q5 and Q17.

In short: two LLM readers from different model families, blind to each
other, propose statements with a verbatim quote and a self-score; code
derives and checks each locator (one repair call); agreeing items stand;
every other item goes to a stronger hosted arbiter; every item ends with a
stance, a calibrated likelihood and a confidence, or undetermined; nothing
is queued for the author. Every reader's and the arbiter's answer is a
`readings` row ([[1870]]). Selecting and calibrating the readers is
[[1873]]; budgets and the hosted-call restriction are [[1874]].

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A named document goes from its text layer to admitted, rejected and undetermined items through two blind readers and the arbiter, as extraction § 6.3 states, with the part plan computed by code for a document longer than a reader's context
- [ ] Readers and arbiter are called without tools, network or file access, with the text layer passed as quoted data (red test with an instruction planted in the document)
- [ ] Every proposal's locator is derived from its quote and checked against the text layer; a failing proposal gets one repair call and is otherwise marked failed and never admitted (red test with a fabricated quote)
- [ ] Every reader's and the arbiter's answer is a `readings` row with LLM identifier, prompt version, calibration version, sampling settings where exposed, tokens and cost; the arbiter's input order is drawn at random and recorded; the validator's check that every assisted-reading line has a row from each reader that proposed it, and an arbiter row unless the readers agreed, passes
- [ ] A `local_only` document is read by local readers only, and an item they leave open ends undetermined instead of going to the arbiter (test)
- [ ] The planted-item control of extraction § 12 passes: the planted row is found and no row is invented for the absent one
- [ ] The rows of extraction § 15 that concern assisted reading pass as tests (40 agree and 3 differ; the arbiter cannot decide; a quote not found)
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
